Fourteen Miles — The Johnstown Flood, 1889 (3D Map Explainer)
Northstar Dizital. Every frame, note and sound made in code; no stock footage, no generated imagery.

FACTS
  U.S. National Park Service, Johnstown Flood National Memorial (nps.gov/jofl): home page and FAQ.
  Johnstown Area Heritage Association (Johnstown Flood Museum), "The Johnstown Flood of 1889".
  Every number with its source and wording: FACTS.md.

MAP DATA (downloads logged in raw/manifest.jsonl)
  Elevation: AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen/Tilezen terrarium; SRTM, NED, GMTED and others), free with attribution.
  Imagery: Sentinel-2 cloudless 2016 by EOX IT Services GmbH (s2maps.eu), CC BY 4.0
           (contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2016).
  River line (Little Conemaugh River) and place positions: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0
           (openstreetmap.org/copyright), via the Nominatim search service. Share-alike applies to the database.
  The 1889 lake: reconstructed from today's terrain (basin behind the dam filled to 491 m; narrow modern fills
           removed from the lakebed). The river stretch from the dam to South Fork is traced on the terrain.
  Map view: a regional view of Pennsylvania; no borders drawn.

TYPE
  Barlow Condensed, The Barlow Project Authors, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL.txt).

VOICE
  Kokoro TTS (kokoro-onnx, Apache 2.0), voice am_michael. Speech check: faster-whisper (MIT).

MUSIC & SOUND
  Original score and procedural foley, made with the Lemo-Opuscar toolkit (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, MIT).
  Instruments sampled from: VS Chamber Orchestra Community Edition (Versilian Studios / Sam Gossner, CC0 1.0)
  and the Versilian Community Sample Library (CC0 1.0). Per-instrument lines: out/instruments.txt.

RENDERING
  three.js (MIT), headless Chromium via Playwright (Apache 2.0), FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL).
